id: pm-rlm-v2parse
title: Tolerant action envelopes and corrective refusal feedback
description: "Diagnose retained cloud response shapes, preserve action schema validation, reject ambiguity and test correction feedback."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-19T05:53:46.263Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-19T13:59:55.544Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Real-shape diagnosis; parser and feedback regressions with behavioral revert proofs
parent: pm-rlm-a1ih
comments[22]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-19T05:54:25.038Z",codex-agent,"Diagnosis before edits: the historical cloud harness deletes scratch ledgers in finally and publishes only response hashes. The 451 glm invalid-action outputs are unavailable, so their shapes cannot honestly be classified. A surviving older local-model ledger contains six exact responses {\"action\":\"finish\",\"answer\":0}; these remain schema refusals. Historical question text conflicted with JSON protocol; merged main already makes questions format-neutral. Plan: wrapper extraction without key coercion, ambiguity refusal, specific correction feedback, recorded-shape regression plus synthetic wrapper edges; retain local-only new-run evidence."
  "2026-10-19T06:00:45.080Z",codex-agent,"Implementation preserves string answer types and rejects duplicate keys, array envelopes, multiple objects and unterminated reasoning. Braces, escaped quotes and reasoning-like text inside JSON strings remain data. Both eval arms share envelope extraction for fair answer formatting. Initial focused suite passes 4/4. Full coverage initially found one untested absent-field branch; added a real-tracker boundary case. Shared eval helpers remove duplicate orchestration without lowering the zero-duplication threshold."
  "2026-10-19T06:01:36.846Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proofs: node test/v2-revert.ts passed 8/8. Parser envelope extraction, corrective feedback, count, sum, distinct, group_count, argmax and argmin each caused its targeted regression to fail with exit 1 when only that production behavior was removed; all source bytes restored. npx pm test pm-rlm-v2parse --run --progress passed both linked commands (focused tests 4/4 plus proofs 8/8). The tracker has result tracking disabled, so this comment is the durable result receipt. Full coverage passed 120/120 tests and 100/100/100/100 over 21 source files."
  "2026-10-19T06:06:53.414Z",codex-agent,"New exact response retained in test/fixtures/glm-5.3-orphan-think.txt: prose, one count JSON example, an unmatched closing think tag, then a second identical count JSON object. It contains no workspace body or answer. The unchanged measured parser refuses this ambiguous envelope; with an explicit opening reasoning delimiter the same content parses. Added that recorded-shape regression without changing production behavior or tuning on answers."
  "2026-10-19T07:17:06.501Z",codex-agent,"Added an exact accepted cloud response fixture: test/fixtures/glm-5.3-prose-action.txt contains prose, a closing reasoning tag in the prefix, then one unique argmax object. Strict JSON.parse refuses it; the measured extractor delivers it without changing its operands. The new positive real-shape regression complements the ambiguous two-object refusal fixture. Production code and prompts remain unchanged; these are response-shape tests, not answer tuning."
  "2026-10-19T07:28:26.501Z",codex-agent,"Final regression receipt: npx pm test pm-rlm-v2parse --run --progress --timeout 900 passed both linked commands: 6/6 focused tests and 10/10 behavioral revert proofs. Each invariant independently fails its regression when removed: parser extraction, fair stuffing extraction, corrective refusal feedback, historical seeded selection, count, sum, distinct, group_count, argmax and argmin. All modified source bytes were restored. Both exact accepted and refused cloud fixtures were verified against retained responses. Ten of thirteen delivered aggregates required envelope extraction."
  "2026-10-19T07:32:37.955Z",codex-agent,"Final verification complete: 6/6 focused regressions, 10/10 independent behavioral revert proofs, and both full release checks at 122/122 plus 2/2 packed consumers each. Two exact new cloud fixtures distinguish a uniquely extractable action from ambiguous repeated objects. The historical cloud strings are unavailable; that evidence gap remains explicit. Claims are being released with items left in progress for orchestrator review."
  "2026-10-19T10:14:44.613Z",codex-agent,"Review round 1: merged main with normal merge drivers. Address parser-version compatibility for replay and resume, URL decoding in the live harness, and a shared validator/schema source for constrained Ollama and OpenAI-compatible output. Preserve the prior evaluation; one newly authorized constrained run uses the same frozen 24 tasks, without answer tuning. Review threads will not be replied to or resolved."
  "2026-10-19T10:19:04.351Z",codex-agent,"Compatibility design: missing parser_version means strict v1; explicit v2 preserves tolerant pre-schema parsing; new checkpoints use v3, whose discriminated union is also the runtime transport validator. Replay, cached responses, fresh resume responses and partition references select the recorded parser. Scope, child-refusal and slice semantic checks remain. Ollama receives format schema; OpenAI-compatible requests use strict json_schema with a generated object wrapper and required nullable optional fields, decoded to canonical actions. Stuffing receives its separate answer schema. Official Ollama docs currently say Cloud structured outputs are unsupported; the single authorized run will measure the requested wire behavior honestly, without retry or model substitution."
  "2026-10-19T10:23:13.591Z",codex-agent,"Revert proofs passed: node test/v2-revert.ts 10/10, including tolerant parser and each of count, sum, distinct, group_count, argmax and argmin. node test/constrained-revert.ts 6/6: checkpoint parser selection, strict v1 parsing, URL decoding, Ollama schema, OpenAI-compatible schema, shared validator. Each regression fails independently with only its behavior removed, then all source bytes are restored. Ajv independently verifies current schema/validator parity across all action alternatives and mutated operands. Initial full coverage attempt identified a missing declaration docstring and two legacy branches; addressed before freezing inference."
  "2026-10-19T10:29:19.233Z",codex-agent,"Current code verification: focused linked suite 14/14; Bun release:check passed 128/128 tests and 2/2 actual packed npm/npx and Bun/bunx consumers, coverage 100/100/100/100 over 22 sources, 82/82 docstrings, zero duplication, production audit and attestation checks. npm ran all 128 tests with full coverage but stopped at stale generated changelog order after tracker updates. Regenerated the changelog; rerun npm gate next. Measured code will now be committed and frozen for the single newly authorized cloud invocation. Linked result persistence is disabled by project policy; this comment retains the receipt."
  "2026-10-19T10:32:52.224Z",codex-agent,"Both full linked release gates now pass on measured source commit 495a156: npm run release:check rerun passed 128/128 tests plus 2/2 packed consumers; Bun likewise 128/128 plus 2/2. Coverage 100/100/100/100 across 22 sources; 82/82 docstrings; zero duplication; production audit, pack allowlist, changelog and attestation checks pass. Fresh no-local clone strict tracker health passes with isolated HOME and no warnings. Normal environment health still reports the external global pm-github host .19 versus pinned .18 skew; package pin and global extension remain unchanged. No SDK defect reproduced. Single constrained live invocation is running against the unchanged committed source."
  "2026-10-19T11:29:07.171Z",codex-agent,"Final compatibility audit corrected strict OpenAI union nodes to omit a redundant object type, so every typed object has closed properties and all fields required. Independent recursive provider-contract regression passes and fails when only this conversion is reverted. Review revert proofs now 7/7 (17/17 including the original 10), with source restored. Native action and answer schema SHA-256 values are unchanged against the fresh measured clone: b5d25da2e58658a436e101bcf6bf9e5fb4177405d61f7898c0cdee5b3e3e0c5a and 8aa6b8e71d80a6b3ca100683098234c23e868630d5c69ef66163e67d8ecb9a7d. No second live invocation; measured revision remains 495a156 and the corrected OpenAI path is unit-tested only."
  "2026-10-19T11:34:33.249Z",codex-agent,"Final full-gate rerun after the strict OpenAI correction passed through linked pm tests: npm run release:check and bun run release:check each pass 128/128 tests and 2/2 actual packed npm/npx and Bun/bunx consumers. Coverage 100/100/100/100 over 22 required sources; 82/82 documented declarations; zero duplication; production audit, pack allowlist, changelog and publish-attestation checks pass. Focused final HTTP/schema suite 8/8 and review revert proofs 7/7, plus original 10/10 proofs. Native schemas match measured commit 495a156 byte-for-byte. PM result recording is disabled by project policy, so comments retain receipts. No SDK bug reproduced; external global extension host skew stays outside the package. PR evidence: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/pull/8 . Claims are released for orchestrator verification; items stay in progress."
  "2026-10-19T12:56:14.874Z",codex-agent,"Review round 2 at eb45b7c: verified wrapper JSON.parse silently accepts duplicate response or nested action keys before canonical validation. Reuse the existing raw-object ambiguity detector before normalization, retaining the original output on refusal so parseAction produces the same invalid code and correction reason. Add wrapper, response, nested argument, escaped-key and valid-output regressions plus independent behavioral revert proof. Replace the stale README pending measurement row with the completed v2 result. No review-thread replies or resolutions."
  "2026-10-19T12:58:07.842Z",codex-agent,"Review round 2 revert proof: node test/constrained-revert.ts passed 8/8. Removing only extractObject(output) from compatibleAction makes the new duplicate-key regression fail with exit 1 (assertion failure); raw wrapper, response, nested filter and array-member duplicates are no longer refused, and corrective feedback fails. All source bytes restored. Focused HTTP/schema suite passes 10/10, including valid wrapped actions, escaped duplicate keys, sibling object keys, typed invalid refusal, charged recovery and deterministic replay. Shared extractor moved unchanged to src/action-envelope.ts to avoid a schema/protocol dependency cycle; protocol preserves its existing export. README now links the completed 24-question v2 result. Thresholds and dependency pins unchanged."
  "2026-10-19T13:12:34.061Z",codex-agent,"Review round 2 npm result: isolated-HOME, empty-global-Git npm run release:check passed all gates, 130/130 tests with zero fail/skip/cancel/todo and 2/2 packed npm/npx and Bun/bunx consumers. Coverage 100/100/100/100 across 23 required sources; 82 documented declarations; zero duplication; production audit clean. Pinned pm focused test execution passed 4/4; tracking_disabled is project policy, so this comment retains results. Known development dependency advisory is already tracked by pm-rlm-wiav; no dependency changes. Bun release:check is running against the unchanged code."
  "2026-10-19T13:15:28.567Z",codex-agent,"Review round 2 final local gates: npm run release:check and bun run release:check each passed 130/130 tests and 2/2 packed npm/npx and Bun/bunx consumers, with zero fail/skip/cancel/todo. Both used isolated HOME and empty global Git settings. Coverage remains 100/100/100/100 across all 23 required sources; 82 documented declarations; 0% duplication; production audit, package allowlist, generated changelog and publish attestation all pass. Review revert proofs passed 8/8; focused HTTP/schema tests passed 10/10; pinned pm linked constrained tests passed 4/4. No new pm defect reproduced. The known development advisory remains in pm-rlm-wiav. Releasing the claim with this item in progress for orchestrator review. PR evidence: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/pull/8 . Review threads remain untouched; no merge or release."
  "2026-10-19T13:46:47.990Z",codex-agent,"Round 3 at head 448e55d: verified both Major findings. Plan: derive one compatible wire schema without minLength, pattern, minimum or maximum while preserving full local validation; verify recorded parse-refusal code and reason before replay or resume. Add real HTTP and real-ledger regressions, prove each fails with only its fix reverted, then run unchanged npm/Bun release gates and regenerate changelog after tracker writes."
  "2026-10-19T13:50:15.485Z",codex-agent,"Round 3 implementation and revert receipts: node --test test/review-r3.test.ts test/constrained.test.ts test/adapters.test.ts passes 12/12. node test/review-r3-revert.ts passes 5/5 independent behavioral reversions: wire keyword removal, adapter wire selection, shared code/message comparison, resume verification and replay verification each make the targeted new regression fail with exit 1 and ERR_ASSERTION; every source is restored byte-for-byte. node test/constrained-revert.ts still passes all 8/8 prior proofs. Real HTTP requests use the stripped schema; local schemaAction/parseAction reject unsupported operands. Real ledgers reject altered or missing refusal reasons, altered codes and null observations for completed and unfinished runs before inference or durable writes. Untampered replay preserves all toon/jsonl bytes. Initial duplication gate caught repeated HTTP fixture parsing; shared test requestBody removes it, keeping the zero threshold."
  "2026-10-19T13:53:07.816Z",codex-agent,"Compatibility audit: origin/main confirms original v1 checkpoints stored code-only refusals. Preserve those original receipts without rewriting them: require the recomputed code, and compare a reason whenever present. Versions 2 and 3 require both fields. The unchanged preexisting legacy regression is retained; new real-ledger coverage rejects changed v1 codes and recorded reasons too. Initial npm release check passed 132/132 plus 2/2 packed consumers and 100/100/100/100; rerun both full gates after this compatibility addition. Pinned pm focused execution passed 2/2; result persistence is disabled by project policy, so comments retain receipts."
  "2026-10-19T13:59:53.149Z",codex-agent,"Round 3 final verification: npm run release:check and bun run release:check both PASS, each with 133/133 tests, zero fail/skip/cancel/todo, and 2/2 actual packed npm/npx and Bun/bunx consumers. Both gates use isolated HOME and empty global Git settings. Unchanged coverage thresholds are met at 100/100/100/100 across all 23 required sources; 86/86 documented declarations; 0% duplication; production audit, pack allowlist, generated changelog and publish attestation pass. Focused HTTP/schema/ledger suite passes 13/13. Pinned pm test execution of both review-r3 commands passes 3/3 new tests and 5/5 independent revert proofs; prior review proofs remain 8/8. Both new regressions demonstrably fail with only their production correction reverted, including independent resume and replay verification bypasses; source bytes are restored. Tests import TypeScript sources directly. Untampered real ledgers replay byte-identically; tampered recorded reasons/codes refuse before inference or durable writes. Original v1 code-only compatibility remains, with every recorded reason compared. Strict tracker health passes with one nonblocking runtime advisory. No new pm CLI/SDK bug or UX gap reproduced; disabled linked-result persistence is existing project policy. No additional live-provider measurement; existing development advisory stays in pm-rlm-wiav. Releasing claim with item in progress for orchestrator verification. PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/pull/8 ; review threads remain untouched."
